<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    ShopFlow.LoadTests — NBomber harness encoding the three sync-engine
    primitives' invariants from 01-product-development-plan.md.docx
    §316–§323 verbatim:

      • Coalescer (§317)       — 100 changes within 500ms → 1 push
      • Per-channel rate limit (§318) — bucket=100/s, 1000 req/s × 5s → 500±5 served
      • Priority queue (§319)  — high-priority job served within 100ms

    The IStockSyncCoalescer / IRateLimiter / IPriorityQueue<T> interfaces
    declared inside this project are SPEC-only placeholders. When U10 /
    Phase-2 Sprint-5 lands the real Channel module
    (ShopFlow.Channel.Application + .Infrastructure), the spec interfaces
    move there and the stubs in this project are replaced with project
    references — a mechanical move, no test rewrites.

    Per Plan §1597 + AGENTS.md §8.59 the load harness runs nightly, NOT
    per-PR. xUnit traits flag every NBomber Fact with
    [Trait("Category", "Load")] so the default per-PR test run filters
    them out via the Category!=Load filter (see Taskfile.yml `test` task
    and the U9 CI workflow when it lands).

    Also hosts k6 scripts under Scripts/ that target the eventual real
    APIs; today they are documentation, scheduled to run nightly once
    U9 wires the dev orchestrator + chaos workflow.

    Inherits all base settings + test conventions from
    Directory.Build.props (root + tests/).
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NBomber" />
    <PackageReference Include="NBomber.Http" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    k6 scripts ship with the test project but are not compiled. Marked as
    None + Pack=false so MSBuild doesn't trip on the .js extension and the
    test runner ignores them.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="Scripts\**\*.js">
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>Never</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Pack>false</Pack>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
